module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.CompletionFullyFaithful.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.ComplementFormalFunctions
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Completion on the complement of a closed subset of a Noetherian affine scheme

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, let `f ∈ 𝔞 ⊆ A` and let `U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)`. Stacks 0EKS asserts
that if `A` is `f`-adically complete and `H¹_𝔞(A)` and `H²_𝔞(A)` are annihilated by powers of
`f`, then the completion functor `Coh(𝒪_U) ⟶ Coh(U, (f)𝒪_U)` of Stacks 0880 is fully faithful on
the finite locally free objects.

The source's proof quotes two lemmas: Stacks 0EKP reduces the assertion to the equality
`Γ(U, 𝒪_U) = lim Γ(U, 𝒪_U/fⁿ𝒪_U)`, and Stacks 0EII supplies that equality. Stacks 0EII is
available here, as `Stacks.Algebraization.ComplementTower.sectionsToLimit_isIso`, and is used as
a theorem; the chain (1) ⇒ (4) of Stacks 0EKP is not, and is carried as the one hypothesis
`hEKP`, stated for every Noetherian ring, every ideal of it and every one of its elements rather
than for `A`, `𝔞`, `f`. The proof instantiates it at `A`, `𝔞`, `f` and discharges both of its
antecedents there: quasi-affineness of `U`, which is proved here, and the equality, which is
Stacks 0EII at the module `A`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Algebraization.complementPrincipalIdealSheaf` — the ideal sheaf `(f)𝒪_U` on
  `U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)`, generated by the restriction of `f` to `U`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.isQuasiAffine_complementZeroLocus_of_isNoetherianRing` — the complement
  of a closed subset of the spectrum of a Noetherian ring is quasi-affine.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.complementPrincipalIdealSheaf_ideal` — over every affine open of `U` the
  ideal of `(f)𝒪_U` is generated by the restriction of `f`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.completionFullyFaithful_of_isAdicComplete_of_annihilated` —
  Stacks 0EKS, granted the chain (1) ⇒ (4) of Stacks 0EKP, which it carries as its one
  hypothesis, general in the ring, the ideal and the element; a special case of
  `Stacks.Algebraization.completionFullyFaithful_of_annihilated`.

## Implementation notes

`U` is quasi-affine because it is a quasi-compact open of an affine scheme: the spectrum of a
Noetherian ring is a Noetherian topological space, so each of its subspaces is compact, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IsQuasiAffine.of_isImmersion` applies to the open immersion
`U ⟶ Spec(A)`. That is the first clause of condition (1) of Stacks 0EKP.

The second clause is the one Stacks 0EII provides. Condition (1) of Stacks 0EKP reads
`Γ(X, 𝒪_X) → lim Γ(Y_n, 𝒪_{Y_n})`, over the infinitesimal neighbourhoods `Y_n` of the closed
subscheme, which is how `Stacks.Algebraization.IsInfinitesimalSectionsComplete` phrases it; the
proof of Stacks 0EKS instead quotes condition (1) in the shape `Γ(U, 𝒪_U) = lim Γ(U, 𝒪_U/fⁿ𝒪_U)`,
which is the shape Stacks 0EII produces and which is
`Stacks.Algebraization.ComplementTower.sectionsToLimit` here. The hypothesis `hEKP` is therefore
the chain (1) ⇒ (4) of Stacks 0EKP read in that second shape, so besides that chain it absorbs
the identification `Γ(Y_n, 𝒪_{Y_n}) = Γ(U, 𝒪_U/fⁿ𝒪_U)` which the source performs silently.

That is the shape which keeps the carried input *single*. Read in the first shape, the chain
(1) ⇒ (4) would still be one hypothesis, but its antecedent would then be
`IsInfinitesimalSectionsComplete`, and discharging that from Stacks 0EII would need the
identification above as a second carried input. So the two shapes are not a choice between a
general hypothesis and a special one: both are stated for every Noetherian ring, every ideal of
it and every one of its elements — `hEKP` quantifies over `B`, `𝔟`, `g`, never mentioning `A`,
`𝔞`, `f` — and the second shape is the one under which a single hypothesis suffices.

### What is missing behind `hEKP`

Of Stacks 0EKP this repository proves only (1) ⇒ (2), as
`Stacks.Algebraization.quasiAffine_sectionsComplete_implies_amplePower_sectionsComplete` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/CompletionFullyFaithful/Basic.lean`, whose
implementation notes list what the remaining implications need: for (2) ⇒ (3), stability of
`Stacks.Algebraization.IsInfinitesimalSectionsComplete` under finite biproducts and under kernels;
for (3) ⇒ (4), the comparison `ℰ/Iⁿℰ ≅ ι_* ι^* ℰ`, whose canonical map is
`Stacks.Algebraization.quotientSubschemeComparisonMap` and which is an isomorphism only once
Stacks 08M3 is available for a closed immersion of schemes. That same comparison at `ℰ = 𝒪_U` is
also what would turn the shape Stacks 0EII produces into condition (1) as
`IsInfinitesimalSectionsComplete` phrases it. It is therefore the single missing input, and it is
what would discharge `hEKP` and let the hypothesis be deleted outright.

Stacks 0EKS itself is proved without `hEKP` as
`Stacks.Algebraization.completionFullyFaithful_of_annihilated` in `AnnihilatedCriterion.lean`,
which imports this module; the version here is a special case of it and carries no Stacks
attribute.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EII](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EII)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0880](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0880)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.LocalCohomology

universe u

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (a : Ideal A) (f : A)

/-- The ideal sheaf `(f)𝒪_U` on `U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)`, generated by the restriction of `f`. -/
public def complementPrincipalIdealSheaf : (complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme).IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {complementTopScalars a f})

/-- Over every affine open of `U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` the ideal of `(f)𝒪_U` is generated by the
restriction of `f`. -/
public theorem complementPrincipalIdealSheaf_ideal
    (V : (complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme).affineOpens) :
    (complementPrincipalIdealSheaf A a f).ideal V =
      Ideal.span {(complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme).presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op
                    (complementTopScalars a f)} := by
  rw [complementPrincipalIdealSheaf, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal, Ideal.map_span,
    Set.image_singleton]

variable [IsNoetherianRing A]

/-- The complement of the zero locus of an ideal in the spectrum of a Noetherian ring is
quasi-affine: it is a quasi-compact open of an affine scheme. -/
@[ega "I 1.1.10" "(ii), special case"]
public theorem isQuasiAffine_complementZeroLocus_of_isNoetherianRing :
    Scheme.IsQuasiAffine (complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme) :=
  have : CompactSpace (complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme) :=
    isCompact_iff_compactSpace.mp (NoetherianSpace.isCompact _)
  Scheme.IsQuasiAffine.of_isImmersion (complementZeroLocus A a).ι

/-- A special case of `Stacks.Algebraization.completionFullyFaithful_of_annihilated`
(Stacks 0EKS), granted the chain (1) ⇒ (4) of Stacks 0EKP: the unconditional statement there
has the same arguments and conclusion and does not need `hEKP`; this version is kept because
that theorem's module imports this one. Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, let `f ∈ 𝔞 ⊆ A` and let
`U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)`.
If `A` is `f`-adically complete and `H¹_𝔞(A)` and `H²_𝔞(A)` are annihilated by powers of `f`,
then the completion functor `Coh(𝒪_U) ⟶ Coh(U, (f)𝒪_U)` is fully faithful on the finite locally
free objects.

The hypothesis `hEKP` is the chain (1) ⇒ (4) of Stacks 0EKP, with condition (1) in the shape the
proof of Stacks 0EKS quotes it: the ambient scheme quasi-affine, and
`Γ(U, 𝒪_U) = lim Γ(U, 𝒪_U/fⁿ𝒪_U)`. It is stated about *every* Noetherian ring `B`, every ideal
`𝔟 ⊆ B` and every `g ∈ B` — none of them `A`, `𝔞`, `f` — so it is a general cited input and not
this theorem's conclusion; compare `hscheme` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isAffine_etale_charts_projective_sections`, the case of schemes of
Stacks 05ID carried the same way under Stacks 0CVY. The proof instantiates `hEKP` at `B := A`,
`𝔟 := 𝔞`, `g := f` and discharges both of its antecedents there: quasi-affineness of `U` by
`Stacks.Algebraization.isQuasiAffine_complementZeroLocus_of_isNoetherianRing`, and the equality
by Stacks 0EII, which is `Stacks.Algebraization.ComplementTower.sectionsToLimit_isIso`, at the
module `A`.

See "What is missing behind `hEKP`" in the module docstring for the one input — Stacks 08M3 —
that would discharge the hypothesis. -/
public theorem completionFullyFaithful_of_isAdicComplete_of_annihilated (hf : f ∈ a)
    (hcomplete : IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {f}) A)
    (h1 : ∃ n, ∀ x : localCohomologyModule A a (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing a)
      (ModuleCat.of A A) 1, f ^ n • x = 0)
    (h2 : ∃ n, ∀ x : localCohomologyModule A a (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing a)
      (ModuleCat.of A A) 2, f ^ n • x = 0)
    (hEKP : ∀ (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing B] (b : Ideal B) (g : B),
      Scheme.IsQuasiAffine (complementZeroLocus B b : Scheme) →
      Function.Bijective (ComplementTower.sectionsToLimit B b g (ModuleCat.of B B)) →
      CompletionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree (complementZeroLocus B b : Scheme)
        (complementPrincipalIdealSheaf B b g)) :
    CompletionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree (complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme)
      (complementPrincipalIdealSheaf A a f) := by
  -- The membership `f ∈ 𝔞` is carried from the source but not consumed, exactly as in
  -- `ComplementTower.sectionsToLimit_isIso`.
  have : f ∈ a := hf
  have := hcomplete
  obtain ⟨c₁, h1'⟩ := h1
  obtain ⟨c₂, h2'⟩ := h2
  exact hEKP A a f (isQuasiAffine_complementZeroLocus_of_isNoetherianRing A a)
    (ComplementTower.bijective_sectionsToLimit a f (ModuleCat.of A A) c₁ c₂ h1' h2')

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
